# The scenes of the parameterised-tests deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# parameterised-tests.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in parameterised-tests.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: the build
note "Parameterised tests come with JUnit Jupiter: nothing to add."
show libs.versions.toml "/^junit/" "gradle/libs.versions.toml"
note "The lesson adds one switch, to choose which calculator the tests run against:"
show lessons/parameterised-tests/example/build.gradle.kts "/^tasks.test/" "lesson build file"

## Scene 2: the code under test
note "The code under test: VAT at 20%. Twenty percent is a fifth, so it divides by five."
show RoundingDownVat 9 12 --zoom 11

## Scene 3: the copy-pasted tests
note "*Copy-pasted* tests: one method per case, and every amount is a round number."
show VatCopyPasteTest 11 28 --zoom 22

## Scene 4: the parameterised test
note "The *parameterised* test: the cases as a table, including every way a fifth of a penny can round."
show VatParameterisedTest 13 30 --zoom 17-24

## Scene 5: the table finds a bug
note "Run the tests against the calculator in use today:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:parameterised-tests:test -Pcode=today"
callout "3 pence net should give 1 penny of VAT, and gives 0. The copy-pasted tests only checked amounts that divide by five."

## Scene 6: the nearest-penny calculator
note "The calculator that rounds to the nearest penny:"
show NearestPennyVat 6 9 --zoom 8
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:parameterised-tests:test"
callout "Every row passes: each case named, each case checked."
